From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:06:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: radio: add a first MT6797 CONSYS FM receiver
 driver

The MT6631 FM receiver has no registers on the AP side. The CONSYS firmware
executes every FM command it gets on STP task 1: register reads and writes,
batches of register operations, and access to the connectivity MCU and the RF
chip's top block. No FM register has been read on this board yet, so it is not
known that the receiver answers.

Add a driver that only finds that out. Probe attaches to the link, switches the
WMT FM function on, runs the vendor's power-up up to its identity check,
reads the identity register three times, runs the vendor's power-down and
switches the function off. It registers no radio device and loads no firmware
file. A command left without an answer skips the power-down, since the block
is then in an unknown state; a CONSYS reload recovers it.

The power-down follows the vendor as written although it is not the reverse
of power-up: it clears a sleep-controller bit in a different register from the
one power-up set, and it leaves the bandgap LDO on.

The event parser keeps its state across link frames and never refuses one,
because a refusal stops the link for every CONSYS client.
---
 drivers/media/radio/Kconfig        |  14 +
 drivers/media/radio/Makefile       |   1 +
 drivers/media/radio/radio-mt6797.c | 462 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 477 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/media/radio/radio-mt6797.c

